    "title": "Starwatch: a rare chance to observe elusive Mercury",
    "summary": "Mercury, the smallest planet and one of the hardest to see because it sits so close to the sun, reached its greatest western elongation on 20 November. That makes this week a rare good chance to spot it in the sky.",
